# Own-wording Tome of Heroes spells, chunk D (Hunting Stand to Less Fool, I). TEXT = {name: text}.
TEXT = {
"Hunting Stand": "You make a camouflaged shelter in the branches of a tree or among a group of stones. It is a 10-foot cube centered on a point within range and holds up to nine Medium or smaller creatures. The inside is comfortable and dry whatever the weather. The camouflage gives its occupants some concealment, so a creature outside has Disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) and Intelligence (Investigation) checks to detect or locate a creature inside.",
"Hypnagogia": "You alter the mental state of one creature you can see within range. It makes an Intelligence saving throw, and a creature with Intelligence 4 or lower is unaffected. On a failure, choose one effect. At the end of each of its turns it repeats the save, ending the spell on a success. Heaviness: crushing fatigue halves its speed and gives it Disadvantage on weapon attacks. Terror: it imagines vivid, frightening hallucinations centered on a point you choose within range. It is Frightened and on each of its turns must Dash away from that point by the safest route, unless it has nowhere to go. Trance: it enters a trancelike state and cannot take Reactions, and rolls a d4 at the start of its turn. 1: it Dashes with all its movement in a random direction (roll a d8). 2: it pantomimes preparing for its day, such as brushing teeth, bathing or eating. 3: it moves up to its speed toward a random creature and makes one melee attack against it, doing nothing if none is in reach. 4: it does nothing. Each time a creature in a trance takes damage, it repeats the save, ending the spell on a success.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can target one more creature for each slot level above 4th, all within 30 feet of each other.",
"Hypnic Jerk": "Between waking and sleeping, a sudden feeling of falling often jolts a person awake. With a snap of your fingers, you trigger that feeling in a creature you can see within range. It makes a Wisdom saving throw or takes 1d6 Force damage. If it fails by 5 or more, it also drops one object it is holding, which lands in its space. The damage rises to 2d6 at level 5, 3d6 at level 11 and 4d6 at level 17.",
"Ill-Fated Word": "You call out a distracting insult to a creature, hurting its chance to succeed. Roll a d4 and subtract the result from an attack roll, ability check or saving throw the target has just made. It uses the lowered result to decide the outcome.",
"Illuminate Spoor": "You touch a set of tracks made by one creature. Those tracks, and all other tracks made by the same creature, give off a faint glow. You and up to three creatures you name when casting can see it. A creature that sees the glow automatically succeeds on Wisdom (Survival) checks to track that creature. If obscuring material such as leaves or mud covers the tracks, you and the creatures you named have Advantage on Survival checks to follow them. If the tracker changes its tracks, such as by adding or removing footwear, the glow stops where they change. Until the spell ends, you can use an action to touch and light up a new set of tracks.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** With a 3rd-level slot, Concentration lasts up to 8 hours. With a 5th-level or higher slot, up to 24 hours.",
"Immolating Gibbet": "You yank up to three creatures you can see within range into the air, their blood turning to fire and burning them from within. Each target makes a Dexterity saving throw or is pulled up to 60 feet into the air and Restrained there until the spell ends. A Restrained creature makes a Constitution saving throw at the start of each of its turns, taking 7d6 Fire damage on a failure or half on a success. At the end of each of its turns it repeats the Dexterity save, and on a success the spell ends on it and it falls, taking fall damage as normal. The Restrained creature, or anyone who can reach it, can instead use an action to make an Intelligence (Arcana) check against your spell save DC. On a success the Restrained condition ends and the creature falls, taking fall damage as normal.",
"Inexorable Summons": "You reach toward a creature and call it. The target teleports to a free space you can see within 5 feet of you. An unwilling creature makes a Wisdom saving throw and is unaffected on a success. You cannot teleport a target into hazards such as lava, and it must land on the ground or a floor.",
"Inspiring Speech": "The verbal component is a rousing speech lasting 10 minutes. When it ends, all your allies within the area who heard it gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls and Advantage on saves against effects that Charm or Frighten for 1 hour. Each recipient also gains temporary hit points equal to your spellcasting ability modifier. If you move farther than 1 mile from your allies or you die, the spell ends. A character can be affected by only one casting at a time, and overlapping castings add nothing and do not extend the duration.",
"Instant Armored Vehicle": "You turn a handful of materials into a Huge armored vehicle of any form you like, with AC 18 and 100 hit points. At 0 hit points it is destroyed. A ground vehicle has a speed of 90 feet, an airborne one has a flying speed of 45 feet, and a waterborne one moves 2 miles per hour. It holds up to four Medium creatures, who have Cover from attacks outside, thanks to arrow slits, portholes and similar openings. A creature piloting it can take the Careen action. The vehicle must move at least 10 feet in a straight line and enter or pass through the space of at least one Large or smaller creature, without provoking opportunity attacks. Each creature in its path makes a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC, taking 5d8 Bludgeoning damage and being knocked Prone on a failure. On a success it may choose to be pushed 5 feet away from where the vehicle passed, and if it declines it suffers the failure. If the pilot is not proficient with vehicles of that kind (land, water or air), each target has Advantage on the save.",
"Instant Snare": "You create a snare at a point you can see within range. You can leave it as a magical trap, or use your Reaction to trigger it when a Large or smaller creature you can see comes within 10 feet. As a trap, a creature must succeed on an Intelligence (Investigation) or Wisdom (Perception) check against your spell save DC to find it. It triggers when a Large or smaller creature comes within 5 feet. The creature makes a Dexterity saving throw or is pulled into the air, Restrained and hanging upside down 5 feet above the snare for 1 minute. A Restrained creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, escaping on a success. Or any creature, the target included, can use its action for an Intelligence (Arcana) check against your spell save DC. On a success the target is freed and the snare resets itself 1 minute later. If the check succeeds by 5 or more, the snare is destroyed instead. If you are within 1 mile when it triggers, you feel a ping in your mind, which wakes you if asleep.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can create one more snare for each slot level above 3rd. When you get the ping, you know which snare triggered.",
"Invested Champion": "You touch a creature and choose to become its champion, or for it to become yours. If your target is your champion, it fights on your behalf. You can cast a touch-range spell on your champion as if its range were 60 feet. Its attacks are magical, and as a bonus action on your turn you can encourage it, giving it Advantage on its next attack roll. If you are the other creature's champion, you have Advantage on attack rolls against creatures that attacked your charge in the last round. If you wield a shield and a creature within 5 feet of you attacks your charge, use your Reaction to impose Disadvantage on the attack, as with the Protection fighting style. If you already have that style, you can also push an enemy 5 feet away from your charge as part of the same Reaction. As a bonus action on your turn, reroll the damage of any successful attack against a creature threatening your charge. In either version, the spell ends if the distance between champion and charge exceeds 60 feet.",
"Iron Gut": "For the duration, one willing creature you touch has Resistance to Poison damage and Advantage on saves against poison. When it makes a Constitution save against an effect that deals Poison damage or would Poison it, it can choose to succeed, and the spell then ends on it. While affected, it gains no benefit from magical foodstuffs such as goodberry or heroes' feast, and suffers no ill effects from harmful nonmagical food such as spoiled food or foul water. Other consumable magic items, such as potions, affect it normally. It can identify poisoned food by a sour taste, and the deadlier the poison, the more sour.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can target one more creature for each slot level above 3rd.",
"Jagged Forcelance": "You create a tether of pulsing golden force between two willing creatures you can see within range, who must be within 15 feet of each other. The tether lasts as long as each tethered creature ends its turn within 15 feet of the other. If one ends its turn farther away, the spell ends. Though it looks like a thin line, its effect covers the full height of the tethered creatures and can affect Prone or hovering creatures that hover no higher than the tallest tethered creature. A creature that touches the tether or ends its turn in a space it passes through makes a Strength saving throw. On a failure it takes 3d6 Force damage and is knocked Prone. On a success it takes half damage and is not Prone. A creature that makes this save, pass or fail, cannot be affected by the tether again until the start of your next turn.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The maximum distance between the tethered creatures grows by 5 feet and the damage by 1d6 for each slot level above 3rd.",
"Jarring Growl": "You loose a growl from deep in your gut that unnerves those who hear it. You have Advantage on Charisma (Intimidation) checks before the start of your next turn. Each creature within 5 feet of you also makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a failure, you have Advantage on attack rolls against it until the end of your turn. You know which creatures failed.",
"Killing Fields": "You call on primal nature spirits to turn natural terrain in a 100-foot cube within range into a private hunting preserve. The area cannot include manufactured structures, and if one exists there, the spell ends. While you are conscious and in the area, you sense the presence and direction, but not the exact location, of each beast and monstrosity there with Intelligence 3 or lower. When such a creature tries to leave, it makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a failure it becomes disoriented, unsure of its surroundings and direction, and stays in the area for 1 hour. On a success it leaves. When you cast the spell, you can name individuals who are helped by the area. All other creatures in it are hindered. You can also set a password that gives its speaker the benefits of being helped. Within the area, a helped creature has Advantage on attack rolls against a hindered creature if a helped, non-incapacitated ally is within 5 feet of the target. Once per turn, when a helped creature hits with a weapon, it deals an extra 1d6 damage of its type to a hindered creature. A helped creature has Advantage on Wisdom (Survival) and Dexterity (Stealth) checks against a hindered creature. Casting this spell in the same place every day for one year makes the field permanent, and structures built there afterward do not end it.",
"Lance": "You create a shimmering lance of force and hurl it at a creature you can see within range. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the target takes 5d6 Force damage and is Restrained by the lance until the end of its next turn.",
"Lay to Rest": "A pulse of searing light bursts out from you. Each undead within 15 feet makes a Constitution saving throw, taking 8d6 Radiant damage on a failure or half on a success. An undead reduced to 0 hit points by this spell disintegrates in a burst of radiant motes, leaving what it wore or carried in the space it occupied.",
"Less Fool, I": "A creature you touch becomes harder to lie to and to influence by magic. Other creatures have Disadvantage on Charisma checks to influence it, and it has Advantage on saves against spells that Charm or Frighten it.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** With a 3rd-level slot, Concentration lasts up to 1 hour. With a 5th-level slot, the duration is 8 hours. With a 7th-level slot, 24 hours. With a 9th-level slot, 1 year. A slot of 5th level or higher removes the need for Concentration.",
}
